  "data_abstract": "STAR-RHIC. Global $\\Lambda$-hyperon Polarization is measured at $\\sqrt{s_{\\rm NN}}=3$ GeV running RHIC/STAR in fixed-target mode. The previously used invariant-mass method is generalized to account for the asymmetries present when operating in this mode. The largest-yet $\\overline{P}_{\\rm H}$ is successfully measured, with nearly 6 sigma of statistical significance. $\\overline{P}_{\\rm H}$ increases with collision centrality, consistent with expectations. No observed dependence on transverse momentum, $p_{\\rm T}$, or rapidity, $y$, is observed.\n",
